Columns:

Candidate Progress Status
Record Count
Current Proposed Days
Median Actual Days
Optimal Proposed Days
Training Month Accuracy %
Validation/Test Month Accuracy %
Mean Absolute Error
Median Absolute Error
Sample Size Flag

MAPPING 2 — INDIA EXTERNAL

Use the same columns.

MAPPING 3 — ROW INTERNAL

Use the same columns.

MAPPING 4 — ROW EXTERNAL

Use the same columns.

STEP 9 — CURRENT VS NEW MAPPING

The workbook may already contain a current Proposed Days mapping.

Compare the current mapping against the newly optimized mapping.

For each of the four segments calculate:

* Current mapping month accuracy
* New mapping month accuracy
* Improvement in percentage points
* Current average absolute error
* New average absolute error
* Current median absolute error
* New median absolute error

I want to know whether the new mapping actually improves prediction accuracy.

STEP 10 — OVERALL RESULTS

Create an Overall Summary table:

Segment | Records | Current Month Accuracy | New Month Accuracy | Improvement | Current MAE | New MAE

The four segments should be:

India + Internal
India + External
ROW + Internal
ROW + External

Also calculate the overall accuracy across all four segments.

STEP 11 — IMPORTANT INTERPRETATION

Do NOT assume that the optimal Proposed Days must equal the mean or median Actual Days.

The Proposed Days must be selected based primarily on the ability to correctly predict the Actual Joining Month.

For example:

If a status has a median Actual Days of 83 but 62 Proposed Days produces better joining-month accuracy, then 62 should be considered the better Proposed Days value.

